WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.901
Everything in the real world
is being recreated

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.267
in the virtual world.

00:00:08.301 --> 00:00:09.434
The metaverse.

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:13.234
The metaverse,
a persistent digital universe

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.501
that mirrors our world,

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.434
but is becoming as diverse
and awe-inspiring

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.834
as the natural world.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.101
And you'll be able to do everything
you do in the real world

00:00:23.101 --> 00:00:24.334
in the virtual world,

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:25.601
and more.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.834
In the real world,
you can walk into a gallery,

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:31.401
buy a one-of-a-kind artwork that is signed
and authenticated as original,

00:00:31.401 --> 00:00:34.367
take it home,
put it on the wall, enjoy it,

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.201
show it to your friends;

00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:37.734
it might even be an investment.

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:43.801
The artwork becomes part of your story
and adds meaning to your life.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.967
It marks a time and a feeling for you.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.267
Now, we can have the exact same experience

00:00:49.301 --> 00:00:51.567
in virtual galleries, with digital art.

00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:55.834
While this might seem
like an obscure niche on the internet,

00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:59.501
let's take a look at a recent auction sale
that you might have heard of.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.667
In March of 2021,

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.767
the major auction house Christie's

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:07.501
sold a purely digital artwork
by an artist named Beeple

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.334
for 69 million dollars in cryptocurrency.

00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:15.567
The auction, the artwork
and the currency was virtual,

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.367
but the transaction was very real.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.434
But who can afford a Beeple?

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:21.001
Don't worry,

00:01:21.034 --> 00:01:23.534
there are lots of artists
creating digital art

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:26.167
and conceptualizing brand new art forms

00:01:26.201 --> 00:01:27.567
that you can afford.

00:01:28.134 --> 00:01:30.634
I direct Media Entrepreneurship
and Innovation

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.001
at the Creative Media Industries Institute

00:01:33.001 --> 00:01:35.201
at Georgia State University,

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:39.034
and our students are building
the metaverse as I speak.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:44.101
We imagine a future where the students
and all digital artists

00:01:44.101 --> 00:01:48.034
are able to continue building
new visions and new worlds --

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.501
basically, a better internet --

00:01:51.101 --> 00:01:53.667
and can make a living while doing so.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.834
The revolutionary instrument

00:01:55.867 --> 00:02:01.334
that allowed for a digital file
to be sold as a unique artwork

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.567
for 69 million dollars

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:07.867
is the same tool that will allow
our students to make livings

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:09.367
as freelance creators.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.634
There is a paradigm shift happening

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:15.634
that is turning the world
of content creation

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.534
and its financial rewards on its head.

00:02:18.201 --> 00:02:22.034
Gone are the days of the internet
being a giant copying machine,

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:26.467
of intermediaries taking
a larger cut than the creators,

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:29.034
and of artists not receiving royalties.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.834
This new automated tool

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:36.901
that allows for guaranteed proof
of origination and ownership

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:41.767
of music, videos, images and even text

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:44.567
is called an NFT:

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:46.001
non-fungible token.

00:02:47.401 --> 00:02:51.334
The NFT is allowing everyone
to own their own data,

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.167
starting with art,

00:02:53.201 --> 00:02:56.034
and there is a hope
that it will revolutionize

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.967
how value is created online

00:02:59.001 --> 00:03:01.334
and how digital labor is monetized.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.401
So the eternal question:

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.567
What is an NFT?

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:07.734
Simply put,

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.734
it is a permanent tracking device

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:12.434
that proves ownership of a digital file,

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.334
somewhat similar to the way
that you can chip a pet

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:19.301
to identify it as yours if it runs away,

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:24.234
an NFT is a cryptographic token
connected to a digital asset

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:27.734
to preserve ownership rights
in the metaverse.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.834
Non-fungible means "not exchangeable."

00:03:31.867 --> 00:03:35.401
Most things in the real world
are non-fungible,

00:03:35.401 --> 00:03:39.234
because most physical objects are unique

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.567
and can't be traded one for one.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:48.601
There is no painting, pet or person
that is exactly equivalent to another.

00:03:50.201 --> 00:03:51.701
Money, on the other hand,

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:55.301
is one of the few items that is fungible,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.634
meaning one dollar is equivalent
to another dollar

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.967
and one Bitcoin is equivalent
to another Bitcoin.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.501
The underlying decentralized technology

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:07.634
that enabled digital currencies
such as Bitcoin

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:08.801
is blockchain.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:14.101
Blockchain prevents digital money
from being duplicated or hacked,

00:04:14.134 --> 00:04:18.734
and it removes the need
for a centralized authority,

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:20.634
such as a bank,

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:21.901
to validate transactions.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:27.201
And like Bitcoin, the record
of ownership of an NFT

00:04:27.201 --> 00:04:30.334
is kept in a public database
on the internet

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.434
that is maintained
by millions of computers

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:35.334
that keep track, via consensus,

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:38.634
of all content origination
and transactions.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:41.101
At the Blockchain Lab
at Georgia State University,

00:04:41.134 --> 00:04:43.667
we study how to monetize creative labor

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:47.401
using blockchains and other
decentralized ledger technologies.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:50.801
I believe that this technology
in the form of NFTs

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:53.667
has the potential to humanize the internet

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:58.667
and to create an equitable foundation
for its next phase: the metaverse.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:03.967
This decentralized business model
gives financial power back to the creators

00:05:03.967 --> 00:05:07.234
and reduces the power
of the broker, the middleman

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:09.567
and even social media platforms.

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:14.334
Amy Rader is a fine artist in Atlanta
who shows in traditional galleries.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.367
She created her first NFT

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:19.367
so that she could expand
to an online audience

00:05:19.401 --> 00:05:22.834
and to add a new revenue stream
to increase her income.

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:25.501
Here's a Greg Mike mural.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:26.701
If you're from Atlanta,

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:30.567
you have probably seen
some of his work on walls and buildings.

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.467
Street art is not permanent,

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:35.967
so how will an important
cultural icon like Greg Mike

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:37.634
utilize this new creative economy?

00:05:39.201 --> 00:05:43.267
He is using the unique qualities
of NFTs to innovate

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:45.801
and to collaborate
with other artists and musicians

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.667
and connect with fans on the internet.

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:49.967
This way, his work will live on,

00:05:49.967 --> 00:05:53.201
and he can take the proceeds
from the sales and resales

00:05:53.201 --> 00:05:55.201
and continue creating his art.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:58.534
Musicians can also capture
their true value

00:05:58.567 --> 00:05:59.701
using NFTs.

00:06:00.034 --> 00:06:02.667
Atlanta music producer Dallas Austin

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:06.767
is allowing fans to collect
memorabilia of his great moments

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:08.101
in music history,

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:11.067
similar to the way that NBA Top Shot

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:16.467
is allowing basketball fans to collect
historical replays as NFTs.

00:06:17.101 --> 00:06:20.634
In the metaverse,
humans are represented as avatars.

00:06:20.967 --> 00:06:22.934
An eight-year-old probably knows,

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:26.234
but did you know that you can buy
clothes for your avatar?

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:27.834
This is Kadine James.

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:29.967
She is leading the way in digital fashion

00:06:30.001 --> 00:06:33.067
that can only be worn
in the virtual world.

00:06:33.101 --> 00:06:37.434
Today, Gucci sells sneakers
that only exist in the virtual world,

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:39.767
and you can never wear them,

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:41.267
but your avatar can.

00:06:41.301 --> 00:06:42.534
Alternatively,

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.101
you can use augmented reality

00:06:44.134 --> 00:06:48.301
to overlay virtual sneakers
onto your in-real-life feet.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.234
And because of NFTs,

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:53.634
anyone, not just well-known
companies like Gucci,

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:59.701
can create digital fashion to be bought,
sold and worn in games,

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.934
online platforms

00:07:01.967 --> 00:07:03.967
and even in avatar fashion shows.

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:07.267
Take the pioneer 18-year-old FEWOCiOUS,

00:07:07.301 --> 00:07:11.901
who was way ahead of Gucci,
with his crypto art and digital sneakers.

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:14.667
The use of augmented
and virtual-reality fashion

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.934
is becoming mainstream,

00:07:15.967 --> 00:07:20.401
but because NFTs as art
and collectibles are so new,

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:23.967
the predictions are too volatile
for anyone to make.

00:07:24.601 --> 00:07:29.367
But it is a sign that heavy hitters
like Mark Cuban and Snoop Dogg

00:07:29.401 --> 00:07:30.867
are investing heavily.

00:07:31.301 --> 00:07:34.101
This is the new frontier
for artists and their fans.

00:07:34.134 --> 00:07:36.367
And just like in the real world,

00:07:36.401 --> 00:07:39.934
and artist can sell a one-of-a-kind piece,

00:07:39.967 --> 00:07:43.067
make limited editions
to control for scarcity,

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:45.601
show in art galleries and market places.

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:48.867
But with NFTs,

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:53.767
you can also sell directly to your buyer
without an intermediary,

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:57.401
collect royalties on all future resales,

00:07:57.401 --> 00:08:00.434
expand your audience
to the entire internet,

00:08:00.467 --> 00:08:04.167
show in virtual galleries
and virtual worlds

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:07.567
and sell 3D objects and clothes
to virtual humans.

00:08:09.034 --> 00:08:10.767
OK, so how does this work,

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:12.834
and how do you get involved as an artist?

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.734
Your artwork is a digital file.

00:08:16.634 --> 00:08:18.334
To protect this file

00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:22.134
and capture the value
of your labor in perpetuity,

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:25.467
you go to a digital goods
marketplace and "mint" it,

00:08:25.467 --> 00:08:31.634
meaning you register your work as a token,
for a fee, on the blockchain.

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:35.567
It will contain a signature, time stamp,

00:08:35.567 --> 00:08:37.701
and any rules around its resale.

00:08:38.867 --> 00:08:42.867
Once you’ve minted your work
and you want to sell it,

00:08:42.867 --> 00:08:44.501
you connect with your community

00:08:44.534 --> 00:08:47.901
and let them know
that your NFT has "dropped,"

00:08:47.901 --> 00:08:49.434
meaning it is for sale.

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:52.467
It is important to note

00:08:52.467 --> 00:08:57.467
that all the same rules
that make for good art and business

00:08:57.501 --> 00:08:59.101
apply in the virtual world:

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:03.501
a strong connection to your followers,

00:09:03.534 --> 00:09:06.401
an authentic or compelling story

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:09.401
and consistent output and work ethic.

00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:13.401
So who will buy your art,

00:09:13.401 --> 00:09:15.767
or how do you get involved as a collector?

00:09:15.801 --> 00:09:19.367
Buyers go to the same
marketplaces that artists use.

00:09:19.401 --> 00:09:22.401
There, you look for art
that you appreciate

00:09:22.434 --> 00:09:24.767
and artists you want
a direct connection with.

00:09:25.734 --> 00:09:29.401
Some people invest because the artwork
resonates with them,

00:09:29.434 --> 00:09:32.067
or they recognize great talent,

00:09:32.067 --> 00:09:38.201
or they see a potential for that artist
to play a significant part in history.

00:09:40.001 --> 00:09:43.634
Once purchased directly from the artist,

00:09:43.667 --> 00:09:46.534
you store your NFTs
in your digital wallet.

00:09:46.567 --> 00:09:47.767
From there,

00:09:47.767 --> 00:09:52.067
you can show on screens
and online marketplaces,

00:09:52.101 --> 00:09:54.867
or in galleries, such as RareRooms,

00:09:54.867 --> 00:09:58.301
a blockchain innovation
by Atlanta's GigLabs.

00:09:58.301 --> 00:10:02.367
And with NFTs, a buyer knows
their art is fair trade,

00:10:02.367 --> 00:10:04.067
transactions are transparent,

00:10:04.101 --> 00:10:06.334
and the ecosystem is equitable.

00:10:06.367 --> 00:10:08.601
The metaverse is a place
where we will spend

00:10:08.634 --> 00:10:10.367
more and more of our lives.

00:10:10.401 --> 00:10:13.734
Who builds it, who owns it
and how it is built

00:10:13.767 --> 00:10:17.034
will determine what this world becomes.

00:10:17.067 --> 00:10:18.934
But just like the real world,

00:10:18.967 --> 00:10:20.967
the metaverse is very complex,

00:10:21.001 --> 00:10:23.801
and there are many problems
yet to be solved.

00:10:23.834 --> 00:10:25.567
And that is where you come in.

00:10:25.601 --> 00:10:26.801
You are the future,

00:10:26.834 --> 00:10:28.267
a digital citizen

00:10:28.301 --> 00:10:33.001
whose responsibility it is
to be a good steward to the metaverse,

00:10:33.034 --> 00:10:38.701
making sure that it is diverse, equitable,
accessible and sustainable.

00:10:40.034 --> 00:10:43.267
This is just the beginning
of the decentralized movement.

00:10:44.301 --> 00:10:48.101
NFTs will revolutionize
most online industries,

00:10:48.101 --> 00:10:50.501
but it is starting
with the creative economy.

00:10:51.867 --> 00:10:54.967
While nothing in this talk
is financial advice,

00:10:55.001 --> 00:10:57.234
it is definitely educational
encouragement.

00:10:57.967 --> 00:11:00.567
And why not start learning through art?

00:11:01.167 --> 00:11:02.334
Jump in.

00:11:02.334 --> 00:11:03.501
We need you.

00:11:04.701 --> 00:11:09.401
I would like to thank the artists
who provided the art for this talk,

00:11:09.434 --> 00:11:12.101
all of which are embedded
in the blockchain

00:11:12.134 --> 00:11:15.067
as NFTs, non-fungible tokens.

